SWEET Mali executable mappings stay inside one 16 MB window (patch 0149): sweet_mali_map takes its GPU VA from mali_va_alloc_map (sweet_mali_pt.h, host-tested), which aligns a SWEET_MALI_EXEC mapping to the next power of two of its size and refuses executable mappings over 16 MB (EINVAL, nothing mapped); data mappings keep 16 KB alignment. One flag translation (mflags) feeds both the VA decision and the page entries. Linux panfrost v6.12 panfrost_gem_open() keeps executable BOs off 16 MB lines with no architecture check ("the program counter is 24-bits"), and panfrost_drv.c matches arm,mali-valhall-jm [src]; its model table has the G57, not the G78, so the invariant is adopted conservatively. Review 1 F1: docs/reviews/mali-exec-16m-review-1.md.
